>And, as I have said before, if you don't care about forgery, it isn't an
>issue for you. What you have just said is that you don't care if
>articles carrying my name are forgeries or not.

Nope. You're trying to apply a "real-world" definition of forgery to Usenet,
and it _doesn't work_; your real-world identity is _irrelevant_, so whether
or not "John Stanley in the real-world" is writing John Stanley's articles,
they are not forged if they are coming from the *same person* who has been
writing them. If someone *else* starts writing articles and posts them
with a "From: stanley@skyking.OCE.ORST.EDU (John Stanley)" header, and 
